    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9fbad082-ea8f-5f4e-b63b-74bee6a001d6" activityNameId="bcaa5d5f-bf54-54da-81d5-522c3883f777" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ventilation system, Alterswohnungen Geeren</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ventilation system, Alterswohnungen Geeren
Production of a ventilation system for a residential care home with apartments and multi-purpose hall. The inventory is based on a building with a total heated gross floor area of 3712 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 6000 m3/h, total weight of the components: 1674 kg/Unit, building with a specific air flow rate of 1.6 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. Data from call of bid including components for air handling units, ducts including insulation, air valves, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers. The data represent a ductwork made of galvanized steel and polyethylene tubes. It includes air handling units mainly with heat recovery. System with central air handling units. Building without ground heat exchanger.;
UUID: 8da9da50-2638-3611-8cc0-2962daa7c170
Materials used for the production. Energy use for the different production steps and for heating the production building. Transport of raw materials to the plant. Estimation for infrastructure of the production site included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology, materials and components used for ventilation systems in commercial and public buildings
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Process information partly from 2003 to 2012
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from call of bids for a ventilation system of a specific building used. Data completed with information from literature and from manufacturers 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8da9da50-2638-3611-8cc0-2962daa7c170.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
